├── book_usage_summary.csv
├── notification_log.csv
│
└── templates/
    └── index.html

Installation:
-Clone the repository:
git clone <repository-url>
cd bookborrowingsystem
-Install dependencies:
pip install pandas flask

Configuration:
Create or update notification_config.py with your email credentials:

SMTP_HOST  = "smtp.gmail.com"
SMTP_PORT  = 587
SMTP_USER  = "your_email@gmail.com"
SMTP_PASS  = "your_app_password"
FROM_NAME  = "Library System"
FROM_EMAIL = SMTP_USER

Usage
1. Generate Reports
python main.py

Outputs:
fine_report.csv
book_usage_summary.csv

2. Send Fine Notifications
python main.py --notify
This sends emails only for late returns.

3. Run Dashboard
python main.py --dashboard

Open in browser:
http://127.0.0.1:5000

Testing:

Run unit tests:
python test_processor.py
python test_notifier.py

Fine Calculation Logic:
Allowed borrowing period: 5 days
Fine is applied only if the book is returned after the allowed period
Fine = (extra days) × (fine per day)
Dashboard Features
View all borrow records
Filter by late/ontime status
Search by user ID, book ID, or record ID
Pagination support
View book usage summary